{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>בגדי שרד [garments of service].</b> These are those mentioned in the section of Numbers Sinai, for HaShem commanded that they cover the Ark with the curtain on account of its honor, and over the curtain a covering of tachash skin, and over this covering an all-blue garment. And by way of reasoning, the blue is on account of the Ark's honor, if the air is clear; and if rain falls he removes it and the tachash-skin covering remains over it. And over the Table of the Presence: a blue garment, and a scarlet garment, and above a tachash-skin covering. And a blue garment over the Menorah and over the golden altar, and purple over the altar of burnt offering, and over all tachash skin. And after he mentioned בגדי שרד, he mentioned בגדי הקדש [garments of holiness], which are for Aaron, who is the High Priest, and he began to explain them:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:54.470476656Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}